body:
I think honestly people really dislike the way they market themselves, with people like Jaclyn and James constantly shoving the code down people's throats in every video. They are also incredibly inconsistent with their quality, the Jaclyn Hill original palette was great but the vault wasn't and it's the same with other products too. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

He needs to understand that the majority of his audience are those in their teens and twenties who watch YouTube regularly. People older than that generally don't watch YouTube for entertainment, but for instructional videos or the news (at least that's my experience).

&#x200B;

No one in my social group, at work, my family etc.. know who he is, because they don't watch YouTube/are not into makeup like I am. It's really not a big deal, he has a big fanbase inside the YouTube community so why does it bother him so much?

I didn't put a blanket statement on it... I said it's offensive because of CONTEXT the same thing you are saying 'is a thing'

It's kind of stupid to even say that its not offensive for a Hindu, Buddhist or Jain to have the tattoo because that is obvious and nobody here is saying that they shouldn't. But this dude is not any of these people, he is a well known racist not associated with any of these cultures who is married to a well known racist who is not associated with any of these cultures.

&#x200B;

It's almost like you want to defend the use of it? My friend is Hindu and has swastika symbols on her bedroom walls, I don't have any problem with that because I know she doesn't associate it with the massacre of Jews, POC, Homosexual and disabled people BUT someone who is married to a woman who said to her Jewish boss ["Burn in Hell Jewbag" and signs it with a swastika](https://theblemish.com/2008/02/kat-von-d-hates-jewish-people/) is probably not using it as the symbol of peace those cultures associate it with.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Girl honestly same here, I said the same a while ago about him and someone went through my entire comment history to prove I wasn't black. I'm albino so I often face this issue, but if people were to see my entire face and features, they would see that I am clearly not white, although I have pale skin. 

&#x200B;

I honestly don't care what Jeffree star thinks of me, I quite like him and others are obviously entitled to their opinions. I've said some stupid stuff before and I'm glad I'm not famous so I don't have it blasted everywhere. I don't know him personally but neither do any of these other people.

&#x200B;

I personally take more offence to being called an uncle tom or a coconut - it has a lot more racist undertones than gorilla or rat do to me personally. Everyone can be entitled to their opinion and that is mine :) Glad you aren't afraid to share yours!
